I have an idea for a new spell, based on the events of the early part
of _The Dragonbone Chair_, by Tad Williams.  Create a new spell that,
when cast, is always instantly fatal, but is *extremely* effective
at destroying everything in an area of effect around the spellcaster.
In TBC the spell is cast by the wizard Morgenes in a small room, killing
guards and causing the room to collapse.  It is described as a fire spell,
invoked by holding orbs or powders in each hand and muttering an
incantation, causing fire to spread from the orbs throughout the body,
generating heat and light, with a final explosion.

It would only make sense to use this spell, of course, if you have
an Amulet of Lifesaving on.  But the effects of the spell on the
surrounding creatures should be more extreme than fighting them
with even the most powerful of weapons and armor -- perhaps destruction
of everything, monsters, objects (including the spellcaster's own
inventory), fountains, and walls, within a 5x5 radius, say.
This would be a desperation move, when surrounded by too many
monsters.


